From 7a497ab2ce68b92dd5a73c060cfbecaddd7dd5c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:17:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sdk): Profile H in the precautionary signature check
 (lifecycle Level 1, H9)

Decryption Authority Lifecycle draft, Profile H rule H9: advisory prechecks
use the same caps, budget and ordering as the verifiers.

- verifyErc1271UserDecrypt takes an optional UserDecryptSignaturePolicy
  (FhevmRuntimeConfig.userDecryptSignaturePolicy). Unset, the check is
  unchanged (ecrecover first, 250,000 gas).
- With a policy: H1 caps on the signature, the transport public key and the
  extra data before any RPC; H3 gas B_exec + 21,000 + 64 x len(calldata);
  H2 ordering `off` (ecrecover first), `shadow` (serves `off`, logs a
  different code-first verdict) or `enforce` (code read at one block: no
  code means a 65-byte ecrecover only; an EIP-7702 indicator means ERC-1271
  with the narrow shim; other code means ERC-1271 only).
- The ethereum module gains optional getCode and getBlockNumber (ethers and
  viem adapters), and eth_call an optional block. A module without them
  forwards under `enforce`, as any inconclusive check does.
- setFhevmRuntimeConfig compares the policy like the other fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
